WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.830
The Last Jedi has been dividing fans since
its release—some fans think it's the best

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.740
installment since The Empire Strikes Back,
while others call it the worst thing to happen

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:10.400
to Star Wars since Jar Jar Binks.

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:14.980
One thing's for sure: it'll be a long time
before anyone can agree on it.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.840
But there must be balance in the Force, so
let's take a look at both the worst and best

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.240
moments from The Last Jedi.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.380
Let's start with the best and work our way
to the Dark Side of The Last Jedi.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.900
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:28.860
Holdo's sacrifice

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.780
Although the various mishaps leading up to
this dramatic scene leave much to be desired,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.400
Vice Admiral Holdo's heroic decision to take
the Resistance flagship on a kamikaze hyperspace

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.780
jump directly into Snoke's ship was one of
the most shocking parts of The Last Jedi.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.920
The amazing visual effects of the collision
made for a particularly impactful moment,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.300
and there's no question that Holdo's selfless
and awe-inspiring maneuver will go down as

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.040
one of the most incredible Star Wars moments
of all time.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.900
Kylo &amp; Rey's fight

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.440
The battle between Rey, Kylo, and Supreme
Leader Snoke's Praetorian Guard was one of

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.580
the definite highlights of The Last Jedi.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:09.540
Sure, many Star Wars fans probably wanted
a traditional lightsaber clash between Kylo

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.740
and Rey, but between the exceptional fight
choreography and the thrill of seeing the

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.420
two come together to defeat Snoke's bodyguards,
this unique battle was a standout moment for

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.820
the movie and the franchise.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.960
Escape from Canto Bight

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.400
While many of Finn and Rose's scenes were
a point of division among audiences, the duo's

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.479
escape from the casino at Canto Bight was
probably the most rewarding part of their

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.200
time together.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:37.810
Aided by slave children, the pair climb aboard
one of the space horses and ride it to freedom,

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:40.240
smashing through the casino and streets in
the process.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:45.440
After being pinned down by the local police
on the cliffside, Rose removes the saddle

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.440
from her Fathier and sets it free.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.060
She and Finn share a moment, reveling in the
damage they did to the wealthy resort city.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.340
Yoda trolls Luke

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.060
Star Wars fans hungry for some original trilogy
nostalgia were probably pleased by the fact

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.950
that practical puppetry effects were used
for Yoda's Force ghost appearance, and Frank

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.900
Oz also returned to voice the character.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:12.560
Also returning for The Last Jedi was Yoda's
trademark quirky sense of humor—a Yoda quite

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.420
unlike the serious Jedi Master seen in the
prequel movies.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.640
Yoda surprises both Luke and the audience
by calling down lightning to strike the tree

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.320
containing the Jedi Order texts.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.800
We later learn that Rey stole the ancient
Jedi texts and hid them aboard the Millennium

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.620
Falcon, but Luke doesn't know that.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:33.060
Yoda's just doing what he did back on Dagobah—teasing
Luke for the fun of it.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:34.400
"haha."

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.320
Luke trolls Kylo

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:41.060
Luke's final scenes in The Last Jedi were
among the best in the entire film.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.780
After mysteriously appearing on Crait, Luke
has a short visit with his sister Leia before

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.660
walking out alone on the salt plain to confront
his nephew.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.980
Luke toys with Kylo, giving Leia and the others
time to escape.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.980
After promising to haunt Kylo and telling
him he will not be the last Jedi, the truth

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:02.680
is revealed: Luke has been using the Force
to project an image of himself across the

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.180
galaxy.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:08.440
Back on his secluded island, Luke passes away
peacefully from the massive effort, presumably

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:09.819
becoming one with the Force.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:14.480
And while these scenes represent the best
of The Last Jedi, there are plenty of moments

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.200
that may have made the audience cringe.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.200
Skywalking

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:23.640
One of the most surprising moments of The
Last Jedi was when Leia uses the Force to

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:27.740
pull herself back through space to the damaged
Resistance flagship.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:31.960
We've never seen Leia use the Force like that--at
least, not in a movie...

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.920
"Now I am a Jedi."

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:41.180
It's long been known that she has the same
potential power as her twin brother, Luke,

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.640
so the concept itself didn't come out of the
blue.

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:48.320
What really made this one of the worst moments
of The Last Jedi was the way it was executed,

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.880
with Leia looking kind of like a sci-fi Mary
Poppins as she flies back into the shattered

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:54.860
bridge of the Raddus.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:04:00.200
It came across a little silly, and we already
had one incredible Mary Poppins scene this

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:00.840
year anyhow.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.820
"I'm Mary Poppins, y'all!"

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.420
Poe's mutiny

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:11.270
After Leia is incapacitated during the attack
on the Raddus, Poe seems surprised when Vice

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.860
Admiral Holdo steps in to command the Resistance.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:19.440
They soon butt heads when Holdo refuses to
tell Poe what her plan is, so Poe impulsively

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.180
sends Finn and Rose on a risky mission with
very little chance of success.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.640
But that's not enough.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:30.759
Later, Poe becomes convinced Holdo is preparing
to abandon ship, and he initiates a mutiny

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:31.260
against her.

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.620
While failure was a major theme of The Last
Jedi, it was extremely painful to watch Poe

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:40.200
fail so badly and get so many people blown
up in the process.

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:41.880
The casino

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.700
Rose and Finn's escape from the casino on
Canto Bight was entertaining, but their time

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:51.460
spent at the gambling den hunting for a master
code breaker was another matter entirely.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:57.580
First, Rose and Finn wear their scruffy Resistance
uniforms in the high class joint and go mostly

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:01.020
undetected until a simple parking violation
gets them caught.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.940
That's unbelievable enough.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:08.200
Then they coincidentally happen to meet a
different code breaker in their jail cell,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:12.100
who just happens to have the same set of skills
as the person they were trying to find.

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.820
While code breaker number two, DJ, ended up
being an interesting character who offered

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:20.939
some important elements to the plot, audiences
couldn't help but wonder why he wasn't the

00:05:20.939 --> 00:05:26.029
main focus of the mission to begin with, instead
of relying on such an implausible coincidence

00:05:26.029 --> 00:05:26.880
to get him involved.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.800
Snoke's exit

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:34.220
One of the most controversial moments from
The Last Jedi is the demise of Supreme Leader

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:35.480
Snoke at the hands of Kylo Ren.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:40.199
The scene itself was played out pretty well,
but some audiences definitely felt let down

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.320
by the Supreme Leader's anticlimactic end.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:48.020
After Snoke was introduced in The Force Awakens,
fans feverishly speculated about Snoke's backstory

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.600
and identity, only to be disappointed when
he kicked the bucket so abruptly.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:57.860
It didn't particularly help that Andy Serkis,
who plays Snoke, fed the speculation by revealing

00:05:57.869 --> 00:06:03.060
tidbits about Snoke's tortured past and implying
he'd have a much larger role to play in the

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:03.560
future.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.560
Rose's heroics

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.660
One of the biggest strengths of The Last Jedi
was its character development.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:14.160
Finn began the film terrified of the First
Order and ready to run, and his only motivations

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.400
are protecting himself and Rey.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:20.640
Meeting Rose and joining her for their abortive
quest teaches Finn a lot about himself and

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.420
what it means to stand up for what's right.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:27.400
By the time the Resistance makes its last
stand on Crait, Finn is a completely changed

00:06:27.409 --> 00:06:32.479
man—one totally ready to give his life for
the cause by going Independence Day on the

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:33.060
First Order.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:37.580
"I'm baaaaaaack!"

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.399
Then Rose saves Finn at the last moment, putting
a quick stop to that redemption arc.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.540
But there were no consequences.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:52.639
Rose survives, and Finn somehow gets her back
across the active battlefield safely, despite

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:57.320
crashing right in front of the whole First
order army and their millions of lasers, leaving

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:59.260
many viewers asking,

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:02.160
"Rose, will you stop being an idiot?"

00:07:02.660 --> 00:07:03.300
Thanks for watching!

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:05.960
